 =?UTF-8?q?he=20desktop=20app=20without=20a=20restart?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
Choose the production desktop renderer root on every protocol request from
<T3 home>/web-override/current, resolved to its real path. Use the override only
when index.html is a file and t3-web-override.json has an appVersion exactly
matching the running desktop app. Otherwise serve the bundled client.

Pass the desktop environment's baseDir and appVersion to protocol registration;
these are the home used by the bundled server and Electron's app.getVersion().
Resolve current once per request, cache validation while its resolved target is
unchanged, and revalidate after target changes or removal. Log invalid or
incompatible targets once each. Placing, switching, rolling back or removing
current takes effect through the existing main-window reload action.

Reuse serveDesktopAsset and confine each resolved file to the selected real
root, rejecting symlink escapes as well as lexical traversal. Preserve HTML
no-store, filename-based immutable caching for hashed assets, other-asset
no-cache, CSP and development proxy behavior. Server HTTP serving is unchanged.

Integration details:
- Preserve upstream early renderer startup and use the same desktop environment baseDir/appVersion supplied to its bundled server; no server protocol or serving changes.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. DesktopApp.ts gained the fresh-install t3 command setup (#33153); packaged builds still pass baseDir and appVersion to registerDesktopProtocol.

